@*
    Whether the empire arrives already ancient.

    A fallen empire is one the galaxy starts with rather than one that grows: enormously powerful,
    dormant, and not a thing the player controls. The designs file has carried spawn_as_fallen all
    along and nothing has ever been able to set it, so an empire written with it kept the setting
    and an empire made here could never have one.

    Stated as the answer rather than as a checkbox, the way portrait duplication is: a box labelled
    "spawn as fallen" leaves you working out what a ticked one means.
*@

<button type="button" class="sem-toggle" aria-pressed="@(Fallen ? "true" : "false")"
        @onclick="() => Session.Edit(d => d.SpawnAsFallen = d.SpawnAsFallen != true)">
    @(Fallen
        ? "Starts as a fallen empire"
        : "Starts as an ordinary empire")
</button>

@code {
    [CascadingParameter]
    public required DesignSession Session { get; set; }

    private bool Fallen => Session.Current!.SpawnAsFallen == true;
}
